== Safe pointers (CANON-25): the run-time check of an owner given away
== (trap 17) stays in the generated code although no accepted program is
== known to reach it. run-tests.sh links this program's Peek with
== owner-check-host.cpp, which calls it with an empty owner (null, as Move
== and Free leave a slot): the program must stop with "use of an owner
== after Move or Free" and exit code 70.
Type
    TNode Struct
        FValue Integer := 0
    ;

Peek(P Own<TNode>) Integer :
    Return P.FValue
;

Main :
    P := New(TNode(FValue := 3))
    PutLn(Peek(Move(P)))
;
